  "findings": [
    "The same firmware programs 78 outbound GDMA links using SPI3 selector 1 in each observed run.",
    "The stock runtime produces no transfer bytes. Changing only the panel GDMA selector restores 153747 bytes and stock Widgets pixels.",
    "The distinct-host candidate retains the original visual output and forwards the same 78 command and data chunks to the panel.",
    "The guest programmed GPIO3 output signal 71 for SPI3 hardware CS0 in all runs. Its old software chip-select state happened to permit the DMA-only playback. This does not verify hardware chip-select behavior in the DMA-only build."
  ],
  "limits": "Private diagnostic runtimes and untouched firmware. Engine inspection is fixed read-only. The screen appeared with Profile, Analytics and Shop tabs, plus the user avatar. No touchscreen, physical hardware or timing-performance claim."
